---
import SectionHeading from "./section-heading.astro";

// Medians on an Apple M1 Pro, end to end through the ultracite CLI. The single
// file is the component from the hero's session; the project is the repo's
// benchmark fixture (`bun ./benchmark/index.ts`, 42 files).
const stats = [
  { label: "Check the file your agent just edited", ms: 330 },
  { label: "Check a whole 42-file project", ms: 333 },
  { label: "The same project on Biome", ms: 249 },
];
---

<section aria-labelledby="hp-fast" class="border-border border-b">
  <div class="hp-frame mx-auto max-w-7xl border-border border-x">
    <SectionHeading id="hp-fast" title="Fast enough to run after every edit">
      Agents check their work after nearly every change. Ultracite answers in
      about a third of a second, so the check never becomes the slow part of
      the loop.
    </SectionHeading>
    <figure class="m-0 border-border border-t">
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 px-4 pt-10 pb-8 sm:px-6 lg:px-10 lg:pt-14">
        <p class="font-mono text-muted-foreground text-xs/5 uppercase tracking-wider">
          One agent turn
        </p>
        <div class="flex h-20 items-stretch gap-1 sm:h-24">
          <div
            class="hatch relative flex min-w-0 flex-1 items-center bg-muted/70 py-2 pr-16 pl-4 ring-1 ring-foreground/10 ring-inset sm:pr-28 sm:pl-6"
          >
            <p class="min-w-0 text-pretty text-[15px]/6 sm:text-base/7">
              <span class="font-medium">Your agent reads, thinks and writes the edit</span>
              <span class="text-muted-foreground max-sm:hidden"
                >{" "}· seconds to minutes, depending on the model and task</span
              >
            </p>
            <span
              aria-hidden="true"
              class="absolute inset-y-0 right-10 w-3 -skew-x-12 border-foreground/25 border-x bg-background sm:right-16"
            ></span>
          </div>
          <div class="w-2.5 shrink-0 bg-signal sm:w-3"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-start justify-end gap-3">
          <p class="text-right text-[15px]/6">
            <span class="font-medium">ultracite check</span>{" "}
            <span class="text-muted-foreground">· 330 ms</span>
          </p>
          <span
            aria-hidden="true"
            class="mr-[3px] h-6 w-px -translate-y-4 bg-foreground sm:mr-[5px]"
          ></span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <dl
        class="grid gap-px border-border border-t bg-border bg-clip-padding sm:grid-cols-3"
      >
        {
          stats.map((stat) => (
            <div class="flex flex-col gap-3 bg-background px-4 py-8 sm:px-6 lg:px-10">
              <dt class="text-pretty text-[15px]/6 text-muted-foreground">
                {stat.label}
              </dt>
              <dd class="order-first font-medium text-5xl tracking-[-0.04em] tabular-nums">
                {stat.ms}
                <span class="ml-1 text-2xl text-muted-foreground tracking-normal">
                  ms
                </span>
              </dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
      <figcaption
        class="text-pretty border-border border-t px-4 py-5 text-muted-foreground text-sm/6 sm:px-6 lg:px-10"
      >
        Agent time isn’t drawn to scale. Check times are medians on an Apple M1
        Pro, end to end through the <code class="font-mono text-[13px]"
          >ultracite</code
        > CLI on Oxlint unless noted: the single file is the component in the session
        above, and the project is the repo’s benchmark fixture (<code
          class="font-mono text-[13px]">bun ./benchmark/index.ts</code
        >).
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>
